Querdian changes (marked "Querdian" in the code):
- package name regexparse;
- a work counter with a budget (parser.work, parser.budget, parser.charge, ErrBudget, ParseBudget);
- the class helpers (appendRange, appendFoldedRange, cleanClass, ...) are methods of the parser, so that
  they can count their work.
- calcSize, calcHeight, repeatIsValid, collapse, factor and the \Q...\E loop count their work too. Each
  loop of parse.go has a comment that says where it is charged or why it is bounded. factor compares
  subexpressions with parser.equal, a counted copy of Regexp.Equal. The other functions of regexp.go
  (String, Equal, MaxCap) do not run in ParseBudget.
